+## Pitfalls
+
+- **Spike becomes production** — the #1 failure mode. If you find yourself cleaning up a spike for production, stop. Write a proper plan with `writing-plans` and rebuild clean.
+- **No observable output** — a spike that only prints "it works" tells the user nothing. Build something they can interact with or see.
+- **Research masquerading as a spike** — if you can answer the question by reading docs, don't build. Spikes are for questions that require building to answer.
+- **Too many spikes** — if you need more than 5 spikes for one idea, the idea is too big. Break it into separate features.
+- **No verdict** — every spike MUST end with a verdict (VALIDATED/PARTIAL/INVALIDATED) and a recommendation. A spike without a verdict is wasted time.
+- **Wrong directory** — create `spikes/` in the repo root, not in `src/` or nested deep in the project. Spikes are standalone.
+- **Comparison spikes not compared** — if you build 002a and 002b, you MUST produce a head-to-head comparison table. Building both without comparing defeats the purpose.
+- **Scope creep** — if the spike starts answering questions beyond the original feasibility question, stop and create a new spike for the new question.
